Hi team, I found `left` function doesn't prune row group as expected,
for example
```sql
memory D ATTACH '/tmp/left_zonemap_pruning.duckdb' AS db (ROW_GROUP_SIZE 2048);
memory D USE db;
-- RG1 → ['0000', '0020'], RG2 → ['0020', '0040'], RG3 → ['0040', '0061']
db D CREATE TABLE left_pruning AS
     SELECT i::INTEGER AS i, lpad(i::VARCHAR, 6, '0') AS s
     FROM range(6144) r(i);
-- we should only r

Hi team, I found prefix doesn't always prune row group as expected, for
example,
```sql
memory D ATTACH '/tmp/prefix_zonemap_pruning.duckdb' AS db (ROW_GROUP_SIZE 2048);
memory D USE db;
db D CREATE TABLE prefix_pruning AS
     SELECT i::INTEGER AS i, lpad(i::VARCHAR, 6, '0') AS s
     FROM range(6144) r(i);
-- no value starts with '00', so no row group should be scanned.
db D EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELE
